Consider the OLO problem in \Cref{def:OLO}. Let the action set $\mathcal X$ has diameter $D=\sup_{\bm x,\bm y\in \mathcal X}\lVert \bm x-\bm y\rVert_1$. Suppose that $\lVert \bm g_t\rVert_\infty\le G_t$, where $G_t$ is some $\mathcal F_{t-1}$-measurable random variable and $(\mathcal F_t)_{t=0}^T$ is the natural filtration, \textit{i.e.}, $\mathcal F_t$ is the $\sigma$-algebra generated by all random observations made during the first $t$ rounds.
Then, \texttt{AdaPFOL}\xspace (\Cref{alg:OLO unbounded}) ensures that for any comparator sequence $\mathring{\bm x}_1,\mathring{\bm x}_2,\ldots,\mathring{\bm x}_T\in \mathcal X$, if $\max_{t\in [T]} G_t\ge 1$, then
