\end{equation*}

As $G$ changes only if $G_t>2\max_{s<t} G_s$, it cannot change for more than $\lceil \log_2 (\max_t G_t)\rceil$ times.
For a fixed $G$, suppose that it is used for rounds $t_1,t_1+1,\ldots,t_2$, then we must have $G_t\le G$, $\forall t\in [t_1,t_2]$ as otherwise a new instance of \texttt{PFOL} will be launched.

Therefore, as $\lVert \bm g_t\rVert_\infty\le G_t\le G$, we have $\lVert G^{-1} \bm g_t\rVert_\infty\le 1$. This allows us to apply \Cref{lem:OLO guarantee} and yield
